A Bitquery investigation on October 30 found that amid the on-chain chaos following the $6.3 billion Binance hack, the proceeds did not remain in the attackers’ hands, but were redistributed by infrastructure providers and arbitrage capital:

Key figures (according to Bitquery; pending cross-verification by multiple parties)
• Validators captured most of the nearly $30 million in payments related to the transactions;
• Attackers tried to prevent the stablecoin issuer from freezing the stolen funds, losing about $119 million on unfavorable trades;
• Trading firms and automated bots exploited price gaps, earning about $60 million after costs;

